    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74226" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύα</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύη</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span> (the latter preferred by
			<i><span class="en">
			Phryn.
			<u>PS</u>
			p.96
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			B.
		</span></i> and more freq. in texts, as <i><span class="en">
			Thphr.
			<u>HP</u>
			3.3.8
		</span></i>, al., but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			3.10.3
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			5.1.2
		</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
			4
		</span></i>), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beech, Fagus silvatica,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Xanth.
				8
			</span></i>, Thphr <i><span class="en">
				<u>HP</u>
				3.3.8
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.10.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dicaearch.
				2.2
			</span></i> ; later, as in Mod. Gr., called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξέα</span></b> , Dosith.<i><span class="en">
				p.396
			</span></i> K., <u>Gloss.</u>, condemned  by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>spear-shaft</i> made from its wood, <i>spear,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				186
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				727
			</span></i>. (Prob. cogn. with ONorse <i>askr</i> 'ash', Lat.
				<i>ornus,</i> etc.)</div>
